# Tests

## Core

- When changing logic, add or update tests in the same style and layout as the project.
- If the area has no tests, say so — don't invent a suite or claim coverage.
- Never claim tests passed without actually running them (or cite why they couldn't run).
- Bar: all relevant tests pass. Cover the changed behavior with meaningful tests — not implementation trivia or coverage-chasing.
- If the project already enforces a coverage threshold, meet it with a real run; don't invent numbers.
- Don't lower the bar — don't skip or delete tests just to make them pass. If public behavior changed on purpose, update the tests to that behavior. Move/extract/rename: extend if needed; don't rewrite assertions only so they pass.
